class.description:
[GrpcClient] speaks real gRPC (HTTP/2) over a plaintext or TLS connection. It supports unary, server-streaming, client-streaming and bidirectional calls. Two API styles are available: - Blocking, compatible with the previous Go GDExtension: [method connect_server], [method invoke], [method invoke_json], [method invoke_server_stream], [method invoke_server_stream_json] and [method last_status]. - Asynchronous Godot-style: [method call_async] returns a [GrpcCall] and [method open_stream] returns a [GrpcStream]. Both run the network exchange on a worker thread. Requests and responses are raw protobuf bytes. The JSON variants use the server's gRPC reflection descriptors, so no generated code is required. [codeblock] var client := GrpcClient.new() client.connect_to_host("127.0.0.1:5051")
var login := JSON.parse_string(client.invoke_json( "/auth.AuthService/Login", JSON.stringify({"username": "alpha", "password": "alpha"}), "{}", 8000))
var session := client.call_async( "/auth.AuthService/Session", PackedByteArray(), {"authorization": "Bearer " + login.data.token}, 8000) await session.completed print(session.get_status()) [/codeblock] [b]Note:[/b] the WASI export template does not include this module: WASI has no outbound sockets.
